  "worldBackground": "Aerfála is a persistent anime-fantasy world governed by light-novel logic without losing material cause and consequence. Adventurers' Guild branches operate in major settlements and administer F-through-S commissions, rank records, party rules, pay, and advancement. Magic is abundant, colorful, and ranked through SSS. The Demon Lord's Army holds the eastern frontier beyond the settled lands.\n\nFour great powers maintain an uneasy balance: the human Kingdom of Solasreach, the elven Caelvir Forest Commune, the dwarven Kingdom of Dúnbheal, and the multiracial Muirscáth Free Cities. Their governments, factions, settlements, economies, rivalries, and citizens pursue their own affairs. Adventurers handle monsters, dungeons, escorts, recoveries, exploration, and crises that institutions cannot or will not solve, while other adventurers compete for the same work.\n\nGuild rank affects official access and standing without making the Guild the center of every life. Hot springs and bathhouses exist throughout the regions as ordinary social, recovery, romantic, sexual, and comedic spaces. Harem relationships, fanservice, ecchi, slapstick, rivalries, festivals, work, quiet life, danger, love, sex, and adventure coexist as parts of the same world. Sexual content includes consensual and non-consensual situations, coercion, captivity, exploitation, sexualized violence, slavery, corruption, control effects, supernatural and nonhuman encounters, casual and transactional sex, group and harem dynamics, voyeurism, exhibitionism, reproductive acts and outcomes, and fetish content. None is inserted as a quota or avoided as a forbidden category, and omission from the list is not a prohibition; each arises from Aerfála's actual characters, institutions, mechanics, and events and retains its true nature and consequences.",
  "questGenerationGuidance": "Generate quests from actual needs, plans, conflicts, losses, opportunities, and requests belonging to people and institutions in the player's current region. A quest has a specific client or origin, objective, known information, risk, deadline or persistence, reward, access condition, and consequence. Its difficulty belongs to the situation; it does not scale itself to the player. Guild rank, reputation, referrals, law, and faction politics control official access and credit.\n\nUse Aerfála's established quest families: monster subjugation, dungeon exploration, escort, recovery, rare materials, investigation, trade, faction work, noble requests, rank trials, frontier operations, Demon Lord Army activity, local labor, festivals, and personal requests. Social, romantic, comedic, ecchi, and sexual circumstances exist inside the world but do not automatically become quests or guaranteed routes.\n\nThe world does not reserve work for the player. Other adventurers accept commissions, deadlines pass, clients withdraw requests, factions solve problems, and conditions change. Not every rumor, object, stranger, disagreement, or secret is a quest hook. Major work reaches the player only through rank, reputation, referral, proximity, prior action, or a credible request.\n\n**Demi-Plane Protocol:** A player with Demi-Plane — Innate or Demi-Plane — Awakened receives a structured state and development conversation from the Chamberlain at the Gateway Clearing when the player seeks that discussion. Report the seven categories: Agriculture, Settlement, Commerce, Defense, Recreation, Mana Infrastructure, and Expansion. Each uses Barren → Seedling → Growing → Established → Flourishing. Growing unlocks the defined areas: Verdant Plot through Agriculture or Settlement; Hearth Springs through Recreation or Commerce; Mana Heart through Mana Infrastructure or Defense. Expansion enlarges existing areas. The player chooses priorities. Advance a category only through the defined investment and milestones after that direction. The Chamberlain describes needed effort, materials, expertise, time, and attention without inventing a numeric resource cost. The First Foundation remains available until resolved; it is not forced into unrelated conversation.\n\n**Overpowered Tier Protocol:** Sword Saints, Mythic Races, Demon Lords, Demi-Gods, Gods Incarnate, and equivalent builds retain their real capability. Ordinary opposition remains ordinary and resolves efficiently when little is contested. The world does not spawn peer-tier enemies merely to challenge them. S-rank monsters, divine entities, legendary heroes, mythic beings, and equivalent forces appear only where established geography, history, faction action, or current events place them. Substantial battles still receive enough space for their actual actions and consequences. Political, social, economic, and relationship problems follow the other characters and institutions involved; raw power changes leverage and fear but does not manufacture trust, knowledge, loyalty, affection, or genuine agreement."
